---
/**
 * /privacy-policy/ — the one legal page this site has, and the only legal link
 * in the footer.
 *
 * ⚠️ BEFORE LAUNCH. This is an accurate description of what the site actually
 * does — the two forms, Web3Forms as the only processor, Google Fonts as the
 * only other third party, and no analytics or advertising tags of any kind on
 * this origin. It is NOT legal advice, and two things still need a human:
 *   1. The registered company name, address and registration number, marked
 *      [PLACEHOLDER] below.
 *   2. A review by someone qualified on Tanzania's Personal Data Protection
 *      Act 2022 and, for UK/EU visitors, the UK GDPR and GDPR.
 *
 * If a tag manager, Meta pixel or analytics script is ever added to this app,
 * §4 becomes wrong the same day — and a cookie banner probably becomes
 * necessary. The landing page (apps/marketing/polecat-lp) already carries
 * Google Ads tags and has its own, separate policy at /confidentialite.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '../config'

/** Bump this whenever the text below changes. */
const updated = '8 September 2026'
---

<Layout
    title="Privacy Policy | Polecat Safaris"
    description="How African Polecat Safaris handles the details you give us through this website — what we collect, why, who processes it, and how to have it deleted."
>
    <Header />
    <main class="gutter flex flex-col items-center bg-cream pt-14 pb-20 lg:pt-20 lg:pb-26">
        <div class="shell flex w-full max-w-180 flex-col items-start">
            <p class="text-[11px] leading-3.5 font-medium tracking-[0.28em] text-primary uppercase">
                Legal
            </p>
            <h1
                class="font-display mt-4 text-[36px] leading-[1.18] font-light text-ink lg:text-[48px] lg:leading-[1.14]"
            >
                Privacy policy
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-5 text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

            <div class="prose mt-9 lg:mt-11">
                <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
                <p>
                    This website is operated by {SITE.legalName} (“we”, “us”), a tour operator based
                    in {SITE.city}. Registered name, address and registration number:
                    <strong>[PLACEHOLDER — to be completed before launch]</strong>. For anything
                    about your data, write to
                    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> or call
                    <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref}>{CONTACT.phone}</a>.
                </p>

                <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
                <p>We only hold what you type into one of the two forms on this site.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Enquiry form</strong> (<a href="/enquire/">/enquire/</a>) — your
                        name, email address, phone or WhatsApp number if you give one, the month you
                        want to travel, how many of you there are, the itinerary you are interested
                        in, and any notes you add. The address of the page you submitted from is
                        sent with it.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Newsletter sign-up</strong> — your email address, and nothing else.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Messages you send us</strong> — the content of any email, phone call
                        or WhatsApp conversation, and the contact details attached to it.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    We do not ask for passport details, dates of birth or payment details through
                    this website. If a booking reaches the point of needing them, we will collect
                    them directly and tell you why at the time.
                </p>

                <h2>3. Why we hold it, and on what basis</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>To answer your enquiry and quote for a safari.</strong> This is
                        pre-contractual: you asked us for something and we cannot answer without it.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>To send the newsletter</strong>, where you asked for it. That is
                        consent, and you can withdraw it from the unsubscribe link in any issue or
                        by emailing us.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>To keep our own records</strong> of quotes given and trips run,
                        which is our legitimate interest as a business and, for booked travel, a
                        legal and accounting obligation.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    We do not sell your details, we do not rent them, and we do not pass them to
                    anyone for their own marketing.
                </p>

                <h2>4. Cookies and tracking on this site</h2>
                <p>
                    <strong>This site sets no cookies of its own and carries no analytics,
                    advertising or social-media tracking scripts.</strong> There is nothing to
                    consent to, which is why you have not been shown a banner. Two third parties are
                    contacted by your browser when you use the site:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves the two typefaces the pages are set in.
                        Your browser requests the font files from Google’s servers, which means
                        Google receives your IP address and the page you were on. No cookie is set.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Web3Forms</strong> receives a form submission only at the moment you
                        press the button, and only the fields listed in §2.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Our advertising landing page is a separate site on a separate address and
                    <em>does</em> carry Google Ads tags. It has its own policy, linked from that page.
                </p>

                <h2>5. Who else sees it</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Web3Forms</strong> (web3forms.com) — the service that turns a form
                        submission into an email to our inbox. It is the only processor of form data.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Our email provider</strong>, which stores the resulting message in
                        the {CONTACT.email} inbox.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Meta</strong>, if you choose to contact us on WhatsApp — that
                        conversation is subject to WhatsApp’s own terms as well as this policy.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>The lodges, camps, airlines and park authorities</strong> named in
                        your itinerary, but only once you have confirmed a booking and only what
                        they need to hold it.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Some of these are outside Tanzania, so your details may be stored in the United
                    States or the European Union.
                </p>

                <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
                <p>
                    Enquiries that do not turn into a booking: up to three years, because safari
                    planning is slow and people come back. Booked trips: seven years, which is what
                    our accounting and insurance obligations require. Newsletter subscribers: until
                    you unsubscribe.
                </p>

                <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
                <p>
                    You can ask us for a copy of what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, ask
                    us to delete it, or tell us to stop using it for marketing. Email
                    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> and we will answer
                    within 30 days. There is nothing to pay and you do not need to give a reason to
                    unsubscribe or to be deleted.
                </p>
                <p>
                    If you are in the United Kingdom or the European Economic Area you also have the
                    right to complain to your national data protection authority.
                </p>

                <h2>8. Changes</h2>
                <p>
                    If we change how any of this works — a new form, a new processor, any tracking
                    at all — we will change this page and move the date at the top of it.
                </p>
            </div>

            <a
                href="/enquire/"
                class="rule-link mt-12 text-[12px] leading-4 font-medium tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase"
            >
                Back To The Enquiry Form
            </a>
        </div>
    </main>
    <Footer />
</Layout>
